  "finalReply": "Saved regex to `/app/regex.txt`:\n\n```\n^(?=[^\\n]*(?<![A-Za-z0-9])(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9]|[0-9])(?:\\.(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9]|[0-9])){3}(?![A-Za-z0-9]))[^\\n]*?((?<![A-Za-z0-9])(?:\\d{4}-(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])|\\d{4}-(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|30)|\\d{4}-02-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]))(?![A-Za-z0-9]))(?![^\\n]*(?<![A-Za-z0-9])(?:\\d{4}-(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])|\\d{4}-(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|30)|\\d{4}-02-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]))(?![A-Za-z0-9]))\n```\n\nHow it meets the spec (`re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)` returns the wanted dates via the single capturing group):\n- **Line contains IPv4:** `^(?=[^\\n]*<IPv4>)` asserts a valid IPv4 exists anywhere ahead on the same line (`.`/`[^\\n]` don't cross newlines).\n- **Last date only:** `[^\\n]*?(<DATE>)(?![^\\n]*<DATE>)` lazily consumes to a date with no valid later date on that line.\n- **Valid dates:** 31-day months `01,03,05,07,08,10,12` allow `01-31`; 30-day months `04,06,09,11` allow `01-30`; `02` allows `01-29` (leap assumption, all years).\n- **Valid IPv4:** octets `25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9]|[0-9]` enforce `0-255` with no leading zeros (`0` alone ok, `01`/`00` rejected).\n- **No false matches:** both dates and IPs are wrapped in `(?<![A-Za-z0-9])` / `(?![A-Za-z0-9])`, so `1134-12-1234`, `a2023-01-01`, `2023-01-01b`, `a192.168.1.1`, `192.168.1.1b` don't count.\n- Only non-capturing groups are used except the one date capture, so `findall` returns date strings.",
